WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:01.970
- [Brittany] When you're
getting on the ice

00:00:01.970 --> 00:00:05.340
and pairs of skaters are
already racing before you,

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:08.020
it can be very, very noisy,

00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:10.780
but the second I step
on the ice for my race,

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:12.270
I become hyper focused.

00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:14.760
My name is Brittany Bowe,

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:17.510
and I am an Olympic
long track speed skater.

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:22.430
- [Narrator] Speed skating
is a competitive sport

00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:24.380
raced around an oval course.

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:27.900
Athletes compete at speeds
up to 36 miles per hour.

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:30.840
The fastest skater wins
and races can be so close,

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:33.890
champions are determined by split seconds.

00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:35.840
While they compete inside
during the Olympics,

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:37.230
athletes train outdoors,

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:39.940
skating in freezing
temperatures and falling snow.

00:00:41.270 --> 00:00:42.960
- [Brittany] The moment
before the gun goes off

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:46.290
is one of the hardest moments of the race.

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:48.220
There's this push-pull that's happening

00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:50.870
because you want to be very calm, relaxed,

00:00:50.870 --> 00:00:51.910
but at the same time,

00:00:51.910 --> 00:00:55.570
you're nervous and your heart
is beating out of your chest.

00:00:55.570 --> 00:00:59.460
My vision and hearing become so narrow,

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:01.810
it sounds like you're
the only person in there.

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:06.410
At this moment, you could
hear a pin drop in the oval.

00:01:06.410 --> 00:01:07.577
- [Man] Ready?

00:01:08.498 --> 00:01:09.830
(gun fires)

00:01:09.830 --> 00:01:11.070
When you're hitting corners,

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:13.600
a gravitational force
feels like it's trying

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:15.660
to pull you right off of the track.

00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:21.330
When you're going around the
track at these high speeds,

00:01:21.330 --> 00:01:24.140
fighting the gravitational forces,

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:27.900
the pain that you feel in
your legs is unimaginable.

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:31.350
It's a sensation of heaviness,

00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:35.670
and it almost feels like
your muscles are suffocating

00:01:35.670 --> 00:01:37.380
because of all of the pressure.

00:01:40.510 --> 00:01:41.820
When you cross the finish line

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:43.850
and you see a number
one next to your name,

00:01:43.850 --> 00:01:45.560
it feels like all of the pain

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:48.030
that I just endured was totally worth it.

